

🚨 Where Could This Break in Production?

1. Data Integrity Issues: Partial Archival
Risk: A record gets uploaded to blob but fails to delete from Cosmos DB — or vice versa.

Impact: Duplicate reads, stale data, incorrect billing analytics.

Mitigation & Fix:

Transactional Semantics: Implement a checkpoint flag or status in the record (archived: true/false) instead of immediately deleting.

Only delete in a second “cleaner” job once the blob version has been confirmed.

Add checksums (e.g., MD5 hash comparison) between Cosmos and Blob versions.

