3. Durable Function Timeouts or Failures
Risk: Orchestration takes too long (e.g., 1,000s of records), causing timeouts.

Impact: Orphaned records or incomplete runs.

Mitigation & Fix:

Implement batching (e.g., 100 records per sub-orchestration).

Use Durable Fan-Out/Fan-In pattern: parallel archival of record batches.

Persist logs in Application Insights to resume incomplete runs.



4. Blob Storage Organization Chaos
Risk: Over time, the folder structure becomes too deep or inconsistent.

Impact: Increased latency when searching for archived records.

Mitigation & Fix:

Enforce a strict naming scheme (e.g., billing-archive/year=YYYY/month=MM/recordID.json)

Optionally maintain a lightweight metadata index in Cosmos or Azure Table Storage to map recordID → blob path.



5. Schema Drift Between Cosmos and Blob
Risk: Your system evolves and the schema of billing records changes over time.

Impact: Consumers may get unexpected data formats from archived records.

Mitigation & Fix:

Save records in blob with versioned schema wrappers:

json
Copy
Edit
{
  "schemaVersion": "v1.2",
  "data": { ... }
}
Keep schema-aware readers that can deserialize old formats or upgrade archived records.


6. Permissions and Secrets Misconfiguration
Risk: A secret rotation or RBAC change causes failures in reading/writing.

Impact: Function fails silently or logs sensitive errors.

Mitigation & Fix:

Use Managed Identity instead of connection strings.

Set up Azure Monitor alerts for failed function runs or 403/401 errors on storage access.

Regularly test disaster scenarios (simulate key revocation).



7. Data Loss Due to Blob Lifecycle Policies
Risk: Blob Storage lifecycle rules might delete old records unintentionally.

Impact: Permanent data loss.

Mitigation & Fix:

DO NOT enable auto-delete lifecycle rules unless explicitly required.

Set immutability policies or configure blob soft delete and versioning to recover from mistakes.



8. Failure to Scale Under Load
Risk: A surge in billing records (e.g., end of month/year) causes function throttling or blob congestion.

Impact: Missed or delayed archival, throttled APIs.

Mitigation & Fix:

Set Cosmos DB throughput to autoscale mode.

Use premium tier storage accounts for faster blob I/O.

Scale out Durable Functions via Elastic Premium Plan or Consumption Plan with concurrency tuning.



9. Loss of Observability
Risk: You can’t trace what happened in case of failure.

Impact: Difficult debugging, slow MTTR (mean time to recovery).

Mitigation & Fix:

Integrate Application Insights for:

Durable Function execution flow

Custom telemetry: records processed, failed, retried

Latency between Cosmos and Blob

Expose a metrics dashboard via Azure Monitor Workbook or Grafana.

