📘 Incident Response Playbook
This outlines how to respond when things go wrong, from alert to resolution, with defined owners and actions.

🆘 1. Incident Types & Severity
Severity	Example	Response Time	Owner
SEV-1	Archived data is inaccessible to users	15 mins	DevOps + Backend
SEV-2	Archival function failed for >12h	1 hour	DevOps
SEV-3	Missing individual records or slow archival	4 hours	Support Tier 2


🔔 2. Alerting Rules (Azure Monitor / App Insights)
Metric	Alert When	Action
Function App failures	≥ 5 failures in 10 min	Auto-open SEV-2
Blob read latency	> 3s p95	Check blob health or CDN fallback
Missing daily archival log	Expected log not found	Trigger SEV-3
Cosmos RU/s saturation	> 80% for 10 min	Scale or analyze hot partitions


🧰 3. First Response Actions
Checklist for On-Call Engineer:

✅ Acknowledge and classify severity.

✅ Check logs in Application Insights.

✅ Identify failing components: Cosmos, Blob, Function, Network.

✅ Restart durable function or retry sub-orchestration if stuck.

✅ Trigger manual archival via script if needed.


