🧾 Day-2 Runbooks
These help with routine operational tasks and recovery procedures.

🔄 Runbook: Reprocessing Failed Archivals
Goal: Retry records that failed to archive or delete.

Steps:
Query Cosmos for records where archived: false and timestamp < now() - 90d

Re-invoke Durable Function manually for those records

Azure CLI Example:

bash
Copy
Edit
az functionapp invoke \
  --name billing-archival-fn \
  --resource-group billing-archival-rg \
  --function-name ReprocessArchive \
  --body '{ "forceRetry": true }'


🔐 Runbook: Rotating Secrets / Credentials
Goal: Safely rotate secrets or keys for Cosmos DB / Blob Storage.

Steps:
Rotate in Azure Portal or via Key Vault.

Update Azure Function app settings:

bash
Copy
Edit
az functionapp config appsettings set \
  --name billing-archival-fn \
  --resource-group billing-archival-rg \
  --settings "COSMOS_DB_KEY=<new_key>" "BLOB_CONN_STR=<new_conn>"

Restart function app to apply changes.

Validate with test archival and blob read.

🧪 Runbook: Testing Disaster Recovery

Goal: Validate that archived records can be recovered and read.

Monthly DR Drill:
Select random month/year blob prefix

Download 10 records

Validate structure and readability

Confirm associated Cosmos records are deleted or marked as archived

🧹 Runbook: Cleaning Orphaned Records

Goal: Identify records that exist in both Cosmos and Blob.

Strategy:
Use a metadata index (if used) or map based on recordID

Flag duplicates

Delete Cosmos copy if blob is valid and checksum matches

